1
00:00:01,969 --> 00:00:03,267
JIM: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,437 --> 00:00:05,406
- I set a bomb.
- Thousands of people could die.

3
00:00:05,572 --> 00:00:07,837
HUGO: <i>Yes. But paying
that price will be better</i>

4
00:00:08,008 --> 00:00:10,102
than releasing
what's down there...

5
00:00:10,477 --> 00:00:12,503
(GROWLING)

6
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:14,542
Are you ready to play?

7
00:00:14,715 --> 00:00:19,483
Wayne Enterprises runs Indian
Hill, but who runs Wayne Enterprises?

8
00:00:19,653 --> 00:00:21,164
BRUCE: <i>There's a
secret council in Gotham.</i>

9
00:00:21,188 --> 00:00:22,486
It's them that wanted me dead.

10
00:00:22,656 --> 00:00:24,136
We're so close to
the ultimate truth.

11
00:00:25,359 --> 00:00:26,725
(YELLING)

12
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:28,120
James.

13
00:00:28,295 --> 00:00:30,628
You did a very bad thing to me.

14
00:00:30,797 --> 00:00:31,837
And now you're going to...

15
00:00:31,999 --> 00:00:33,524
- (BLOWS)
- (GASPS)

16
00:00:34,201 --> 00:00:38,468
- Impossible.
- (TUTTING) Nothing is impossible.

17
00:00:41,241 --> 00:00:42,937
(SNARLING)

18
00:00:43,143 --> 00:00:44,202
Thank you.

19
00:00:44,378 --> 00:00:45,938
Bruce, I might not
see you for a while.

20
00:00:46,013 --> 00:00:47,106
Where are you going?

21
00:00:47,281 --> 00:00:48,442
I have to find Lee.

22
00:01:02,796 --> 00:01:04,526
(DR. THOMPKINS LAUGHING)

23
00:01:41,168 --> 00:01:43,103
(GLASS SHATTERING)

24
00:01:43,704 --> 00:01:46,105
(ALARM BLARING)

25
00:01:53,246 --> 00:01:54,441
MAN: Hello?

26
00:01:57,451 --> 00:01:58,612
We're closed.

27
00:02:04,591 --> 00:02:07,186
If you leave now I
won't call the cops.

28
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:09,786
(OBJECTS CLATTERING)

29
00:02:22,876 --> 00:02:23,876
(GROWLING)

30
00:02:29,016 --> 00:02:30,382
(SCREAMING)

31
00:02:37,057 --> 00:02:38,218
JIM: Hey.

32
00:02:40,494 --> 00:02:42,486
Any chance you
wanna come quietly?

33
00:02:47,734 --> 00:02:49,259
(GROWLING)

34
00:02:49,469 --> 00:02:51,267
(JIM GRUNTING)

35
00:03:00,313 --> 00:03:01,313
(GROANS)

36
00:03:04,384 --> 00:03:05,384
(LAUGHS)

37
00:03:29,142 --> 00:03:31,168
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

38
00:03:34,347 --> 00:03:36,543
- (CAMERAS CLICKING)
- (INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

39
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:47,194
At 8:15 this evening,

40
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:50,228
an individual robbed a
pharmacy and attacked its owner.

41
00:03:50,397 --> 00:03:52,025
<i>While we don't
have an ID as yet,</i>

42
00:03:52,199 --> 00:03:56,227
we believe that this individual is
another escapee from Indian Hill.

43
00:03:56,403 --> 00:03:58,599
How much do you know
about other escapees?

44
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:02,141
FEMALE REPORTER 1: <i>Are
these monsters dangerous?</i>

45
00:04:02,309 --> 00:04:03,986
FEMALE REPORTER 2:
<i>Captain Barnes! Captain Barnes!</i>

46
00:04:04,010 --> 00:04:05,672
Valerie Vale, <i>Gotham Gazette.</i>

47
00:04:05,846 --> 00:04:07,371
Why can't we see the escapee?

48
00:04:07,547 --> 00:04:09,948
Because crews are still
picking up the pieces.

49
00:04:10,117 --> 00:04:13,417
This isn't the first time that a bounty
hunter has apprehended an escapee.

50
00:04:13,587 --> 00:04:16,216
Is the GCPD incapable of
handling this threat themselves?

51
00:04:16,389 --> 00:04:20,156
Whoa. Only a handful of these escapees
have been brought in by bounty hunters.

52
00:04:20,527 --> 00:04:23,122
The vast majority were
apprehended by GCPD.

53
00:04:23,296 --> 00:04:24,355
Yes. True that.

54
00:04:24,531 --> 00:04:27,899
Excuse me. Excuse me. I
take issue with the word "threat."

55
00:04:28,068 --> 00:04:33,063
These escapees are themselves
victims of Hugo Strange.

56
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:35,835
Now, if any ordinary,
hard-working citizen

57
00:04:36,009 --> 00:04:38,240
wants to help get these
poor souls off the street

58
00:04:38,411 --> 00:04:40,778
so that they may
receive proper treatment,

59
00:04:40,947 --> 00:04:43,109
<i>well, these citizens
should be lauded.</i>

60
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:44,683
And rewarded financially.

61
00:04:44,851 --> 00:04:46,945
Mr. James, before they
were taken to Indian Hill,

62
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:49,612
these "poor souls" were
all criminally insane inmates

63
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:52,089
at Arkham Asylum, were they not?

64
00:04:53,527 --> 00:04:54,551
Next question.

65
00:04:54,728 --> 00:04:57,664
Hear that? You should be lauded.

66
00:04:57,831 --> 00:04:59,390
I'll settle for the cash.

67
00:04:59,566 --> 00:05:02,126
How many escapees have
you brought in now, hmm? Six?

68
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:04,294
Five grand a pop,
that's not too bad.

69
00:05:05,038 --> 00:05:06,638
What happens when
there aren't any more?

70
00:05:06,706 --> 00:05:09,232
I don't think Gotham's running
out of monsters anytime soon.

71
00:05:09,409 --> 00:05:11,776
I really can't get you
to come back, huh?

72
00:05:11,945 --> 00:05:14,210
Look, whatever happened
when you went to see Lee,

73
00:05:14,381 --> 00:05:15,906
and you know I
don't like to pry...

74
00:05:16,082 --> 00:05:17,243
Sure you do.

75
00:05:17,417 --> 00:05:19,061
That's because you
won't tell me anything.

76
00:05:19,085 --> 00:05:21,111
The whole point is, man's
not supposed to be alone.

77
00:05:21,288 --> 00:05:22,654
You have a family here.

78
00:05:22,823 --> 00:05:24,189
Can't do it, Harv.

79
00:05:24,357 --> 00:05:26,656
But you've got no problem
chasing down Strange's freaks.

80
00:05:26,827 --> 00:05:27,920
Yeah. It pays the rent.

81
00:05:28,094 --> 00:05:30,290
You are a cop in
everything but name.

82
00:05:30,463 --> 00:05:32,523
Yeah. Except I don't
have to listen to Barnes.

83
00:05:32,699 --> 00:05:35,225
I get to go home when I
want. Get drunk when I want.

84
00:05:35,402 --> 00:05:40,204
And at the end of the day, I sleep, 'cause
saving Gotham's not my job anymore.

85
00:05:40,373 --> 00:05:42,467
Jim, I love you like a brother.

86
00:05:42,642 --> 00:05:45,168
But you've got to
stop blaming the job

87
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:48,213
for what happened
between you and Lee.

88
00:05:48,381 --> 00:05:50,873
And do you really think I
don't get drunk when I want?

89
00:05:51,051 --> 00:05:52,051
(CHUCKLES)

90
00:05:53,753 --> 00:05:56,484
Detective Bullock, I looked into
the drug the escapee was after.

91
00:05:56,656 --> 00:05:59,626
It's a powerful immune
suppressant. Gordon.

92
00:05:59,793 --> 00:06:01,056
See, look at Lucius here,

93
00:06:01,228 --> 00:06:03,857
our new resident expert
on all things scientific.

94
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:07,330
He said sayonara to the
Wayne Enterprises robots, hmm?

95
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:08,627
And he loves it here.

96
00:06:10,303 --> 00:06:12,829
Wayne Enterprises revealed
itself as morally corrupt.

97
00:06:13,006 --> 00:06:16,306
Here, despite the
primitive facilities,

98
00:06:16,476 --> 00:06:18,638
casual violence, fascistic
meathead culture...

99
00:06:18,812 --> 00:06:19,905
Lucius.

100
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:21,639
I love it.

101
00:06:21,815 --> 00:06:25,047
Anyway, that drug is only sold
at three pharmacies in the city.

102
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:27,597
And the other two pharmacies
were both robbed in the last month.

103
00:06:27,621 --> 00:06:31,422
Question is why are Indian Hill
escapees now robbing pharmacies?

104
00:06:31,591 --> 00:06:32,650
BULLOCK: <i>Good question.</i>

105
00:06:32,826 --> 00:06:34,727
So what do you say,
just like the old days,

106
00:06:34,895 --> 00:06:36,659
you and me run it
together, huh, partner?

107
00:06:37,664 --> 00:06:40,862
You get a hard lead on an escapee,
and the price is right, I'll bring him in.

108
00:06:42,202 --> 00:06:44,797
Thanks for the drink. Lucius.

109
00:06:46,206 --> 00:06:48,072
"Fascistic meathead culture"?

110
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:50,721
I mean, you couldn't try to
be just a little bit more positive?

111
00:06:50,844 --> 00:06:52,813
- I was very positive.
- Uh-huh.

112
00:06:54,648 --> 00:06:56,392
Why is Hugo Strange the
only one that's been arrested?

113
00:06:56,416 --> 00:06:57,475
The situation...

114
00:06:57,651 --> 00:07:00,196
What about the rumors that Indian
Hill is a Wayne Enterprise facility?

115
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:02,031
<i>And how many more of
these escapees are at large?</i>

116
00:07:02,055 --> 00:07:04,889
Are we talking 20? Thirty? Come
on, just give me a blink if I'm close.

117
00:07:05,058 --> 00:07:07,857
The situation is firmly in hand.

118
00:07:08,028 --> 00:07:09,223
MAN: <i>Liar!</i>

119
00:07:11,564 --> 00:07:12,827
Oh, no.

120
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:16,592
My name is Oswald Cobblepot.

121
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:20,229
We know who you are,
Penguin. What do you want?

122
00:07:20,407 --> 00:07:22,501
COBBLEPOT: <i>What do I want?</i>

123
00:07:22,676 --> 00:07:25,407
I want you to tell the truth
to the people of Gotham.

124
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:28,940
<i>They would have us believe
that there is no danger.</i>

125
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:33,553
But I was there the night those
creatures broke out of Indian Hill.

126
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:36,087
I saw them.

127
00:07:36,256 --> 00:07:38,350
And I saw who was leading them.

128
00:07:38,525 --> 00:07:40,494
Are you saying the
escapees are organized?

129
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:42,595
Hello. That is what I am saying.

130
00:07:42,762 --> 00:07:45,254
There is absolutely
nothing to support that.

131
00:07:45,432 --> 00:07:46,866
I told the police
who to look for.

132
00:07:47,033 --> 00:07:50,197
I begged them. Time and again.

133
00:07:50,370 --> 00:07:53,067
And they have done nothing.

134
00:07:53,940 --> 00:07:58,002
So, I am here to speak directly

135
00:07:58,178 --> 00:08:01,444
to the good people of Gotham.

136
00:08:02,549 --> 00:08:06,145
The enemy's name is Fish Mooney.

137
00:08:06,886 --> 00:08:10,288
BARNES: <i>Fish Mooney? She hasn't
been spotted for over six months.</i>

138
00:08:10,457 --> 00:08:13,484
She's either long
gone, or she's dead.

139
00:08:14,861 --> 00:08:17,262
I wish I shared
your simple belief.

140
00:08:18,698 --> 00:08:22,226
She is a criminal.
She is a murderer.

141
00:08:22,402 --> 00:08:26,464
And now, God knows what kind of
monster Hugo Strange has turned her into.

142
00:08:26,639 --> 00:08:29,905
<i>I implore every
citizen of Gotham.</i>

143
00:08:30,076 --> 00:08:34,172
If you love your family,
if you love your children,

144
00:08:35,915 --> 00:08:37,884
find Fish Mooney.

145
00:08:38,752 --> 00:08:41,620
Until then, no one is safe.

146
00:08:44,591 --> 00:08:46,753
(REPORTERS CHATTERING)

147
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:49,389
MAN: <i>Hey, Penguin.</i>

148
00:08:53,033 --> 00:08:54,296
Hello, Jim.

149
00:08:55,402 --> 00:08:56,665
Oswald.

150
00:08:57,670 --> 00:09:00,037
I'm surprised you
haven't found Mooney.

151
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:02,232
I hear you're quite the
bounty hunter these days.

152
00:09:04,911 --> 00:09:06,743
You haven't made
it worth my while.

153
00:09:08,248 --> 00:09:10,843
Oh, tough guy now.

154
00:09:11,017 --> 00:09:12,610
But he makes a point.

155
00:09:20,727 --> 00:09:22,753
(MUSIC PLAYING)

156
00:09:44,217 --> 00:09:47,051
Ozzie, Butch.

157
00:09:47,220 --> 00:09:50,384
What a nice surprise.

158
00:09:50,557 --> 00:09:52,219
Forgive me for
not coming sooner.

159
00:09:52,392 --> 00:09:55,487
- The place looks marvelous.
- Hmm.

160
00:09:55,695 --> 00:09:56,993
Wouldn't you say so, Butch?

161
00:09:57,163 --> 00:09:58,722
Yeah. Place looks great.

162
00:09:58,898 --> 00:10:02,892
I imagine you're here about your offer,
to let us shelter under your umbrella?

163
00:10:03,069 --> 00:10:04,349
I only want what's best for you.

164
00:10:04,504 --> 00:10:06,268
I appreciate the thought.

165
00:10:06,439 --> 00:10:08,374
But we're big girls.

166
00:10:08,541 --> 00:10:10,169
We can handle ourselves.

167
00:10:10,944 --> 00:10:12,003
Can't we?

168
00:10:13,246 --> 00:10:14,339
Sure we can.

169
00:10:14,514 --> 00:10:15,880
Hey, Butch.

170
00:10:17,550 --> 00:10:19,917
Hey. How're you doing?

171
00:10:20,086 --> 00:10:21,247
You taking care of yourself?

172
00:10:21,421 --> 00:10:25,449
Yeah. Yeah. So,
how're you doing?

173
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:27,423
You already asked her that.

174
00:10:27,827 --> 00:10:30,956
(CLEARS THROAT) Listen, you
guys should take him up on his offer.

175
00:10:31,131 --> 00:10:32,963
Gotham's full of
rough characters.

176
00:10:34,033 --> 00:10:36,059
You look great. By the way.

177
00:10:37,570 --> 00:10:39,562
Wait over there. Please.

178
00:10:42,041 --> 00:10:44,704
Poor bunny. Break-ups are hard.

179
00:10:45,912 --> 00:10:47,403
I offered to kill you.

180
00:10:48,381 --> 00:10:49,940
I thought it would
raise his spirits,

181
00:10:50,116 --> 00:10:54,076
and would be my pleasure seeing
as how you murdered my mother!

182
00:10:54,254 --> 00:10:57,850
But he is nursing some foolish hope
that you two will get back together.

183
00:10:59,292 --> 00:11:00,817
Love.

184
00:11:00,994 --> 00:11:02,554
You can take your
offer and stick it...

185
00:11:02,729 --> 00:11:04,254
We'll think about it, Ozzie.

186
00:11:05,999 --> 00:11:07,262
Fine.

187
00:11:07,433 --> 00:11:09,595
But that's not the
only reason I'm here.

188
00:11:09,769 --> 00:11:10,828
Spread the word.

189
00:11:11,004 --> 00:11:13,803
I want Fish Mooney,

190
00:11:13,973 --> 00:11:18,069
and I will give a million dollars
to whoever can bring her to me.

191
00:11:19,279 --> 00:11:22,044
Dead, or alive.

192
00:11:22,215 --> 00:11:23,843
Chopped into pieces.

193
00:11:26,619 --> 00:11:27,780
I want her.

194
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:35,521
You okay, Butch?

195
00:11:36,996 --> 00:11:38,589
World getting you down?

196
00:11:38,898 --> 00:11:40,696
Uh, I am fine, kid.

197
00:11:40,867 --> 00:11:43,393
And you're too young
to be in here. Scram.

198
00:11:43,770 --> 00:11:46,035
Yeesh. Just trying to be nice.

199
00:11:49,309 --> 00:11:51,471
Just seein' her
kills me. You know?

200
00:11:54,647 --> 00:11:55,740
Get over it.

201
00:11:55,915 --> 00:11:58,214
And that child just
stole your wallet.

202
00:12:01,788 --> 00:12:03,154
(CAT YOWLING)

203
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:04,849
Hey.

204
00:12:05,024 --> 00:12:07,084
Barbara and that whip
lady are gonna get angry,

205
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:09,092
you stealing from
their customers.

206
00:12:09,262 --> 00:12:11,163
Let 'em. I've got
other things goin'.

207
00:12:11,331 --> 00:12:13,766
- Like what?
- Top secret.

208
00:12:13,933 --> 00:12:15,026
Let's eat. I'm starving.

209
00:12:15,201 --> 00:12:18,797
Hey, kid. Take it. It's yours.

210
00:12:19,706 --> 00:12:22,574
You keep feeding strays, and
one's gonna follow you home.

211
00:12:22,742 --> 00:12:25,109
Like you? Come on.

212
00:12:32,352 --> 00:12:34,344
Well, that should
be the last of it.

213
00:12:35,054 --> 00:12:36,886
I'll put the kettle on.

214
00:12:37,056 --> 00:12:38,752
There is nothing like
a sweet cup of tea

215
00:12:38,925 --> 00:12:41,394
to make home feel like
home after a long trip away.

216
00:12:41,561 --> 00:12:42,859
Eh, Master Bruce?

217
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:47,028
You all right?

218
00:12:52,639 --> 00:12:56,406
Were we right to leave, Alfred?
Stay away all of this time?

219
00:12:56,576 --> 00:12:58,487
Well, considering the
appalling state of the topiary,

220
00:12:58,511 --> 00:13:00,275
I should say
absolutely-bloody-not.

221
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:01,812
Alfred, you know what I mean.

222
00:13:03,916 --> 00:13:06,078
I know you know why we left.

223
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:09,354
We had to leave.

224
00:13:09,522 --> 00:13:11,388
You're nervous about
tomorrow, aren't ya'?

225
00:13:11,557 --> 00:13:12,581
Yes.

226
00:13:12,759 --> 00:13:14,853
Well, you wouldn't be
human if you weren't.

227
00:13:15,028 --> 00:13:18,294
So, why don't you go through
there, take a pew. Help your feet up.

228
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:21,957
And I'll see about that
lovely cup of tea. All right?

229
00:13:40,887 --> 00:13:42,651
Saving that for someone special?

230
00:13:49,095 --> 00:13:50,358
Coffee please.

231
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:55,927
"Search continues for new
Arkham Asylum director."

232
00:13:56,102 --> 00:13:59,595
Right. Good luck finding
anyone to take that job.

233
00:13:59,772 --> 00:14:01,452
I'm Valerie Vale.
Reporter for the <i>Gazette.</i>

234
00:14:01,607 --> 00:14:03,098
I know who you are.

235
00:14:03,276 --> 00:14:06,508
And you're James Gordon.
Son of a respected Gotham DA.

236
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:10,639
Former war hero. Former white
knight cop. Now bounty hunter.

237
00:14:10,817 --> 00:14:12,494
You know, someone
should do a story on you.

238
00:14:12,518 --> 00:14:14,077
Not interested.

239
00:14:14,253 --> 00:14:15,744
Yeah. Me neither, actually.

240
00:14:16,756 --> 00:14:18,436
You were there that
night, at Indian Hill.

241
00:14:18,558 --> 00:14:19,787
I've got nothing to say.

242
00:14:19,959 --> 00:14:23,191
What about the fact that besides
Hugo Strange and his assistant,

243
00:14:23,363 --> 00:14:24,592
no one else has been arrested?

244
00:14:24,764 --> 00:14:27,757
Or that despite everything
pointing to Wayne Enterprises,

245
00:14:27,934 --> 00:14:29,800
there seems to be
zero investigation.

246
00:14:29,969 --> 00:14:31,494
You're new to
Gotham, aren't you?

247
00:14:31,671 --> 00:14:33,982
Okay. This is where you tell
me things work differently here?

248
00:14:34,006 --> 00:14:36,840
I'm not from Gotham. But my
dad's a cop. My brothers are cops.

249
00:14:37,009 --> 00:14:38,602
And things work the
same everywhere.

250
00:14:38,778 --> 00:14:42,476
I was going to say, it's hard
to find a quiet bar in this city.

251
00:14:42,648 --> 00:14:45,880
I like coming here. Please
don't make me find another.

252
00:14:46,052 --> 00:14:48,317
Now, do you think
Cobblepot's right,

253
00:14:48,488 --> 00:14:50,480
that Fish Mooney's
organizing the escapees?

254
00:14:50,656 --> 00:14:52,852
Penguin is a liar
and a murderer.

255
00:14:53,126 --> 00:14:55,425
Hmm. But?

256
00:14:56,829 --> 00:15:02,359
But, based on the escapees,
and knowing Fish, I hope not.

257
00:15:06,172 --> 00:15:10,268
Well, he's offering a million
dollars to whoever brings her in.

258
00:15:12,612 --> 00:15:13,875
You're welcome.

259
00:15:36,202 --> 00:15:37,568
It's a puzzle.

260
00:15:38,871 --> 00:15:40,863
The trick is opening it.

261
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:43,703
<i>The man at the store said it's
one of the most difficult ever made.</i>

262
00:15:43,876 --> 00:15:47,369
People pass it down
unsolved for generations.

263
00:15:49,749 --> 00:15:51,945
A mathematician
once went mad trying...

264
00:15:56,756 --> 00:15:58,247
Yes.

265
00:15:58,424 --> 00:16:00,416
Well, there you go. (LAUGHS)

266
00:16:00,860 --> 00:16:02,351
It was a lovely thought.

267
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:05,928
And did you get the biscuits?

268
00:16:06,732 --> 00:16:08,894
And the sweater? I know
how drafty these rooms are.

269
00:16:09,068 --> 00:16:10,502
- Mr. Penguin...
- Oswald.

270
00:16:10,670 --> 00:16:12,350
- When I think how I treated you...
- Stop.

271
00:16:13,406 --> 00:16:14,999
Why are you being so kind?

272
00:16:17,109 --> 00:16:19,601
Talking to you
these past months,

273
00:16:21,047 --> 00:16:23,482
I don't know how I
would've gotten by otherwise.

274
00:16:25,585 --> 00:16:28,054
With Fish out there
planning who knows what.

275
00:16:29,655 --> 00:16:32,090
Me being surrounded
by morons and lunatics.

276
00:16:32,258 --> 00:16:33,783
I know the feeling.

277
00:16:37,396 --> 00:16:39,236
Why didn't she kill me
when she had the chance?

278
00:16:40,733 --> 00:16:42,099
I was powerless.

279
00:16:43,269 --> 00:16:47,468
She must have a larger goal. I
need to know what she is doing.

280
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:49,131
Do you?

281
00:16:57,783 --> 00:17:00,446
When Alexander
encountered the Gordian knot,

282
00:17:00,620 --> 00:17:03,055
a knot so complex no one had
ever been able to untangle it,

283
00:17:07,059 --> 00:17:10,826
he just removed his sword
and cut it in two. (CHUCKLES)

284
00:17:11,497 --> 00:17:13,295
<i>Details can be distracting.</i>

285
00:17:13,466 --> 00:17:17,904
Sometimes, a
simple solution is best.

286
00:17:19,205 --> 00:17:21,333
So no matter what
she is planning,

287
00:17:21,507 --> 00:17:22,998
just remember...

288
00:17:27,046 --> 00:17:32,075
Penguins eat fish.

289
00:18:11,724 --> 00:18:13,215
You know why we're here.

290
00:18:17,063 --> 00:18:19,589
What are you doing
here? Stop. Stop.

291
00:18:19,799 --> 00:18:20,799
(GASPS)

292
00:18:31,744 --> 00:18:36,045
So, what are we after? It's
not like they keep cash around.

293
00:18:36,215 --> 00:18:37,740
For now, survival.

294
00:18:37,917 --> 00:18:38,976
Don't move.

295
00:18:40,853 --> 00:18:42,913
Hands.

296
00:18:43,089 --> 00:18:44,284
Hands.

297
00:18:47,827 --> 00:18:49,159
Of course.

298
00:18:55,735 --> 00:18:57,135
Drop the gun.

299
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:02,331
Now knock yourself out.

300
00:19:07,279 --> 00:19:09,805
That was awesome. How did you...

301
00:19:11,183 --> 00:19:14,176
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Fish.

302
00:19:14,353 --> 00:19:17,016
I'm fine. Watch the door.

303
00:19:21,527 --> 00:19:24,691
Yeah, that's the only company
that makes the drug. Fray Pharma.

304
00:19:24,864 --> 00:19:26,958
<i>They actually have a
warehouse here in Gotham.</i>

305
00:19:27,133 --> 00:19:28,453
You think they
could be a target?

306
00:19:28,501 --> 00:19:30,868
JIM: <i>Yeah, they're the only
pharmacy that carries the drug.</i>

307
00:19:31,037 --> 00:19:33,233
If somebody wants it, they'll
have to go to the source.

308
00:19:33,406 --> 00:19:35,238
Let me find the address.

309
00:19:35,408 --> 00:19:36,569
<i>That's all right.</i>

310
00:19:59,865 --> 00:20:01,595
James Gordon.

311
00:20:01,767 --> 00:20:03,258
Hands where I can see 'em.

312
00:20:04,403 --> 00:20:05,803
So, what?

313
00:20:05,971 --> 00:20:09,032
You're here to collect the bounty
that Penguin has over my head?

314
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:11,905
What is it, a million dollars?

315
00:20:12,078 --> 00:20:14,775
And to think I
let that punk live.

316
00:20:14,947 --> 00:20:19,544
Well then, I think
you'd better cuff me.

317
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:21,981
Cuff yourself.

318
00:20:23,355 --> 00:20:25,085
How many others
you have with you?

319
00:20:25,257 --> 00:20:26,885
They're all with me.

320
00:20:27,059 --> 00:20:31,258
Every wretched soul that
Hugo Strange experimented on.

321
00:20:31,430 --> 00:20:33,422
But tonight, just him.

322
00:20:38,437 --> 00:20:39,437
(GRUNTING)

323
00:21:22,214 --> 00:21:24,726
Did you hear them rats last
night, scurrying around in the attic?

324
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:25,945
Drove me bloody-bonkers.

325
00:21:27,019 --> 00:21:29,231
Now, may I ask you, what's
the point of having a caretaker

326
00:21:29,255 --> 00:21:31,247
if they can't take
care of nothing, eh?

327
00:21:33,058 --> 00:21:35,084
You all right, Master B?

328
00:21:36,095 --> 00:21:39,361
Hungry. I should've eaten.

329
00:21:39,532 --> 00:21:40,864
Excuse me, gentlemen.

330
00:21:46,839 --> 00:21:49,035
I do this, there's
no turning back.

331
00:21:50,709 --> 00:21:51,870
No.

332
00:21:54,046 --> 00:21:55,537
You say your piece.

333
00:21:57,316 --> 00:22:00,150
We'll see about getting you
a proper breakfast, all right?

334
00:22:13,933 --> 00:22:15,973
I'd like to thank the board
for giving me this time.

335
00:22:17,937 --> 00:22:20,417
It will come as no surprise
I'd like to talk about Indian Hill.

336
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:25,441
I know preliminary investigations have
concluded Hugo Strange acted alone.

337
00:22:26,812 --> 00:22:28,110
I reject this conclusion.

338
00:22:30,249 --> 00:22:32,209
While trapped in Indian
Hill, I was led to believe

339
00:22:32,351 --> 00:22:35,150
an unnamed group had
taken control of my company,

340
00:22:35,321 --> 00:22:37,347
and it was they who
hired Hugo Strange.

341
00:22:38,824 --> 00:22:40,349
<i>I left Gotham both
for my own safety,</i>

342
00:22:40,526 --> 00:22:43,471
and so that I might have the time to
discover hard evidence of their existence.

343
00:22:43,495 --> 00:22:48,991
(SCOFFS) A conspiracy
theory? That's why we're all here?

344
00:22:49,835 --> 00:22:51,599
Excuse me, Master Bruce.

345
00:22:51,770 --> 00:22:53,762
Pardon me, sir. Might I
have your name please?

346
00:22:53,939 --> 00:22:57,137
- What?
- Your name. Please, sir.

347
00:22:59,712 --> 00:23:00,771
Crowley.

348
00:23:00,946 --> 00:23:04,542
Mr. Crowley, did your parents
never teach you any manners?

349
00:23:04,717 --> 00:23:06,447
I don't have to listen to this.

350
00:23:06,619 --> 00:23:08,349
Oh, but you do, sir.

351
00:23:08,520 --> 00:23:11,547
That is precisely the
point that I am making.

352
00:23:13,525 --> 00:23:14,788
I know how it sounds.

353
00:23:17,129 --> 00:23:18,893
But I now have proof they exist.

354
00:23:21,767 --> 00:23:23,360
And I can tell you
that they're here.

355
00:23:25,237 --> 00:23:26,671
In this room.

356
00:23:31,744 --> 00:23:33,940
I want to talk face-to-face.

357
00:23:34,113 --> 00:23:36,691
You have 24 hours to contact me,
or the information that I've gathered

358
00:23:36,715 --> 00:23:39,310
will be sent to every newspaper
and television station in Gotham.

359
00:23:42,021 --> 00:23:43,512
Thank you for your time.

360
00:23:49,161 --> 00:23:51,858
- Pancakes?
- Pancakes.

361
00:23:58,037 --> 00:23:59,835
WOMAN: And how
did the board react?

362
00:24:01,273 --> 00:24:03,265
Then he leaves us no choice.

363
00:24:10,282 --> 00:24:11,443
Bruce Wayne.

364
00:24:12,985 --> 00:24:14,385
<i>Do it quietly.</i>

365
00:24:29,702 --> 00:24:30,931
(WHISTLES)

366
00:24:42,715 --> 00:24:44,650
- You Barbara Kean?
- We're closed.

367
00:24:48,253 --> 00:24:49,312
What?

368
00:24:50,289 --> 00:24:52,656
You built this club
on our territory.

369
00:24:52,825 --> 00:24:55,624
We let you 'cause we
heard Penguin had your back.

370
00:24:55,794 --> 00:24:57,057
And now we hear that ain't so.

371
00:24:57,329 --> 00:24:58,329
Oh.

372
00:24:59,331 --> 00:25:01,857
Bad for you. Good for us.

373
00:25:03,502 --> 00:25:04,765
Get the hell out.

374
00:25:04,970 --> 00:25:05,970
(BARBARA GRUNTS)

375
00:25:07,439 --> 00:25:09,704
This place is ours now.
Do you understand?

376
00:25:09,875 --> 00:25:11,434
You can't just come in here...

377
00:25:11,610 --> 00:25:13,340
Don't hit me, okay? Please.

378
00:25:13,545 --> 00:25:15,411
(SOBBING)

379
00:25:16,915 --> 00:25:18,713
(LAUGHING)

380
00:25:37,136 --> 00:25:38,136
(GRUNTS)

381
00:25:48,480 --> 00:25:50,039
- Hey.
- Hey.

382
00:25:50,215 --> 00:25:52,415
You still paying for stuff
about the Indian Hill freaks?

383
00:25:53,218 --> 00:25:55,380
Depends. If it's good.

384
00:25:56,088 --> 00:25:57,750
Is Fish Mooney good?

385
00:26:09,268 --> 00:26:11,169
Guess I'm finding a new bar.

386
00:26:11,336 --> 00:26:12,580
I heard you ran into
Fish Mooney yesterday.

387
00:26:12,604 --> 00:26:13,663
So?

388
00:26:13,839 --> 00:26:16,274
So, are you still
interested in finding her?

389
00:26:16,475 --> 00:26:18,842
Every cop in the city
is looking for her now.

390
00:26:19,711 --> 00:26:21,873
But I know where
she's gonna be next.

391
00:26:22,848 --> 00:26:24,476
And why are you telling me?

392
00:26:24,650 --> 00:26:26,278
You see, I need
something from the cops.

393
00:26:26,452 --> 00:26:29,251
They're not gonna tell me.
But Bullock still trusts you.

394
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:30,912
And you want me to lie to him.

395
00:26:31,090 --> 00:26:33,252
A million dollars
covers a lot of sins.

396
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:35,394
<i>And obviously, I
get to come along.</i>

397
00:26:36,128 --> 00:26:38,563
<i>Aw, don't tell me you
have a conscience?</i>

398
00:26:38,730 --> 00:26:39,891
Yeah, all right.

399
00:26:46,738 --> 00:26:48,639
Jimmy. Hey.

400
00:26:48,807 --> 00:26:50,605
So, after your run-in with Fish,

401
00:26:50,776 --> 00:26:53,041
Barnes had us up all night,
rousting her old hideouts.

402
00:26:53,212 --> 00:26:54,339
Yeah. Did you find anything?

403
00:26:54,513 --> 00:26:56,277
Nada. But I did get
what you asked for.

404
00:26:58,016 --> 00:26:59,496
You wanna tell me
what this is about?

405
00:26:59,651 --> 00:27:01,381
It's a hunch. Probably nothing.

406
00:27:01,553 --> 00:27:03,465
Look, if you've got a hot
lead you don't wanna share

407
00:27:03,489 --> 00:27:06,049
so you can collect Penguin's
million, I got no problem with that.

408
00:27:06,091 --> 00:27:08,424
Just don't get yourself
killed or me fired, okay?

409
00:27:08,594 --> 00:27:10,927
I'll do my best. Hey.
Get some rest, huh?

410
00:27:14,967 --> 00:27:16,026
Hey.

411
00:27:23,442 --> 00:27:25,377
When did you get back?

412
00:27:25,544 --> 00:27:26,705
A couple days ago.

413
00:27:28,380 --> 00:27:30,144
I tried to find
you before I left.

414
00:27:30,315 --> 00:27:32,147
No worries.

415
00:27:32,317 --> 00:27:34,809
You remember what I
discovered that night at Indian Hill,

416
00:27:34,987 --> 00:27:38,048
that there was a secret group
that had infiltrated my company.

417
00:27:38,223 --> 00:27:39,885
I wasn't paying attention.

418
00:27:40,058 --> 00:27:42,137
I needed time to research
them. I couldn't do it here.

419
00:27:42,161 --> 00:27:43,459
Okay.

420
00:27:43,629 --> 00:27:45,598
I have a plan, but these
people are powerful.

421
00:27:45,764 --> 00:27:47,724
We need to assume they
know you and I are friends.

422
00:27:47,866 --> 00:27:49,226
- You need to be careful.
- Got it.

423
00:27:49,334 --> 00:27:50,734
- I'm serious.
- I can see that.

424
00:27:56,074 --> 00:27:57,599
I'm sorry I was
gone for so long.

425
00:27:57,776 --> 00:27:59,404
Don't apologize.

426
00:28:00,078 --> 00:28:03,606
Shoot, if I could fly to Italy and
eat pizza all day I would, too.

427
00:28:03,782 --> 00:28:05,808
- Switzerland.
- Italy's better.

428
00:28:05,984 --> 00:28:08,613
- Selina...
- Bruce, seriously.

429
00:28:08,787 --> 00:28:10,483
Don't sweat it.

430
00:28:10,656 --> 00:28:14,058
I gotta go. I'll see you around.

431
00:28:17,029 --> 00:28:18,429
Good to see you, Selina.

432
00:28:34,746 --> 00:28:36,681
- Hey, did you get her?
- Yeah.

433
00:28:36,848 --> 00:28:38,968
She was under guard in a
building on Douglas and 80th.

434
00:28:39,084 --> 00:28:41,212
There's one thing though.

435
00:28:41,386 --> 00:28:44,379
Hey. Hey! What the
hell are you doing?

436
00:28:44,556 --> 00:28:46,301
You're a hundred yards
from a police station.

437
00:28:46,325 --> 00:28:47,565
I'll be back in an hour or two.

438
00:28:47,626 --> 00:28:48,650
We had a deal.

439
00:28:48,827 --> 00:28:50,693
If there's a story, I'll
make sure you get it.

440
00:28:50,862 --> 00:28:52,296
Oh, you're a son of a bitch.

441
00:28:52,464 --> 00:28:55,434
Also, you could scream, but then
you'd have to tell the cops everything,

442
00:28:55,601 --> 00:28:57,001
and you'd lose
the story entirely.

443
00:28:57,169 --> 00:28:59,661
Gordon. Gordon!

444
00:29:00,505 --> 00:29:01,505
You son of a bitch.

445
00:29:15,187 --> 00:29:17,349
Forty-Seven, this is dispatch.

446
00:29:17,522 --> 00:29:18,800
FEMALE OFFICER:
<i>This is Forty-Seven.</i>

447
00:29:18,824 --> 00:29:20,520
Report to Captain
Barnes immediately.

448
00:29:20,692 --> 00:29:22,854
Relief team will take
your place. Over and out.

449
00:29:23,028 --> 00:29:24,519
<i>You got it. We're out of here.</i>

450
00:29:37,542 --> 00:29:38,908
(SIREN BLARING)

451
00:29:46,585 --> 00:29:47,609
(KNOCK ON DOOR)

452
00:29:55,627 --> 00:29:56,822
I knocked.

453
00:29:56,995 --> 00:29:58,429
I didn't answer.

454
00:29:59,631 --> 00:30:00,758
You alone?

455
00:30:00,932 --> 00:30:02,992
All day, every day.

456
00:30:03,168 --> 00:30:06,263
I wasn't expecting
Jim Gordon to stop by.

457
00:30:06,438 --> 00:30:09,101
You aren't supposed
to be here, are you?

458
00:30:09,274 --> 00:30:11,402
How come you're not in jail?

459
00:30:11,576 --> 00:30:15,377
I agreed to testify
against Professor Strange.

460
00:30:15,547 --> 00:30:19,541
In case you're about to ask, I
don't know who really ran Indian Hill.

461
00:30:20,752 --> 00:30:23,051
I don't care who
ran Indian Hill.

462
00:30:23,221 --> 00:30:24,814
Then why are you here?

463
00:30:27,159 --> 00:30:28,252
Fish Mooney.

464
00:30:28,427 --> 00:30:31,955
And why would I know
how to find Fish Mooney?

465
00:30:32,130 --> 00:30:34,156
No reason you would.

466
00:30:34,333 --> 00:30:37,735
But it's clear whatever you and
Strange did to her is making her sick.

467
00:30:37,903 --> 00:30:41,738
Her people are stealing drugs,
but I don't think they're working.

468
00:30:41,907 --> 00:30:43,933
She's gonna come after you.

469
00:30:44,109 --> 00:30:47,511
Or her goons will, and
they'll lead me to her.

470
00:30:47,679 --> 00:30:50,911
And how will they find me? Only
the police are supposed to know.

471
00:30:51,083 --> 00:30:54,076
My guess, she'll have someone
get the information for her.

472
00:30:54,252 --> 00:30:59,020
Someone who wouldn't suspect
being used. Maybe a reporter.

473
00:31:04,196 --> 00:31:08,395
<i>She will follow that person, or
whoever she goes to for help.</i>

474
00:31:08,567 --> 00:31:12,868
In this case, a bounty
hunter, right to you.

475
00:31:13,572 --> 00:31:14,572
(DOOR SQUEAKING)

476
00:31:16,341 --> 00:31:20,711
You led them to me on
purpose. You're using me as bait.

477
00:31:20,879 --> 00:31:24,281
I don't like being played. Plus,
she's worth a million dollars.

478
00:31:47,706 --> 00:31:51,507
No! Gordon, help!
Somebody, help!

479
00:32:41,293 --> 00:32:44,491
I don't know which one of you I wanna
bat over the head with this cane more.

480
00:32:45,630 --> 00:32:46,757
I get it.

481
00:32:47,466 --> 00:32:49,560
Life disappointed you.

482
00:32:49,734 --> 00:32:52,568
So what? Does that
make you special?

483
00:32:52,737 --> 00:32:53,830
I'm done with you.

484
00:32:54,005 --> 00:32:55,166
You cross me again,

485
00:32:55,340 --> 00:32:58,572
I will have you skinned alive
and your head put on a pike.

486
00:32:58,743 --> 00:32:59,870
And you.

487
00:33:01,713 --> 00:33:06,344
When I came back, I saw the way
you handled things while I was away.

488
00:33:06,518 --> 00:33:08,714
I swear, I had this
feeling right here.

489
00:33:09,988 --> 00:33:11,854
I thought I was
having a heart attack.

490
00:33:12,023 --> 00:33:14,959
But it was pride,
Bullock. In you.

491
00:33:15,126 --> 00:33:20,292
The next time I have that
feeling, I'll know it was just gas.

492
00:33:21,867 --> 00:33:24,166
You both better
pray that we find her.

493
00:33:26,271 --> 00:33:27,466
Get out of my sight.

494
00:33:32,978 --> 00:33:34,412
(COUGHING)

495
00:33:35,714 --> 00:33:37,307
I'd say that went well.

496
00:33:38,183 --> 00:33:40,709
He was right though.
About me being Captain.

497
00:33:40,886 --> 00:33:42,650
I did a good job.
I even liked it.

498
00:33:42,821 --> 00:33:47,282
Yeah. Hey, look, I'm sorry, Harvey.
I'll do my best to find Peabody.

499
00:33:47,459 --> 00:33:50,520
Honestly, Jim,
for the time being,

500
00:33:50,695 --> 00:33:54,462
it might be better if
you just stayed away.

501
00:33:56,535 --> 00:33:58,299
Hey. Hey!

502
00:34:00,372 --> 00:34:01,372
Ow.

503
00:34:01,640 --> 00:34:04,405
- Just tell me. Did you know?
- Did I know what?

504
00:34:04,576 --> 00:34:06,670
That Mooney was
using us to find Peabody.

505
00:34:06,845 --> 00:34:09,872
You mean using you?
Yeah, it's her kind of play.

506
00:34:10,649 --> 00:34:12,049
- You should've told me.
- Sure.

507
00:34:12,217 --> 00:34:13,897
Why didn't you tell me
who your source was?

508
00:34:15,720 --> 00:34:17,814
That's it? You're not
gonna try and find Mooney?

509
00:34:19,591 --> 00:34:22,425
Barnes is on it. I've had a
long day. I'm gonna get a drink.

510
00:34:23,695 --> 00:34:24,754
Gordon.

511
00:34:28,733 --> 00:34:29,792
Nothing.

512
00:34:36,207 --> 00:34:38,767
- Come on.
- I said no.

513
00:34:38,944 --> 00:34:41,106
- Who are they?
- Just people.

514
00:34:41,279 --> 00:34:42,713
They need me to
do things for them.

515
00:34:42,881 --> 00:34:44,179
Well, I can do stuff.

516
00:34:45,684 --> 00:34:48,848
These are scary people,
okay? It's for your own good.

517
00:34:49,020 --> 00:34:50,818
You just don't wanna share.

518
00:34:50,989 --> 00:34:53,390
Just stay here, all right?

519
00:35:00,765 --> 00:35:01,858
Hello.

520
00:35:02,834 --> 00:35:04,097
What do you want?

521
00:35:05,036 --> 00:35:06,402
I want to talk to her.

522
00:35:07,639 --> 00:35:09,164
I was following her.

523
00:35:10,508 --> 00:35:11,601
She was kind to me.

524
00:35:12,777 --> 00:35:15,212
But then, she met him, that boy.

525
00:35:15,380 --> 00:35:17,144
What happened to you?

526
00:35:17,916 --> 00:35:19,282
You know me?

527
00:35:19,451 --> 00:35:20,783
Uh, yeah. I know Bruce Wayne.

528
00:35:20,952 --> 00:35:22,284
Who is he? Who is he?

529
00:35:22,454 --> 00:35:23,894
What's wrong with
you? Let go of me.

530
00:35:23,989 --> 00:35:28,359
Bruce Wayne. Bruce
Wayne. Who is he?

531
00:35:31,830 --> 00:35:33,628
I really do not
have time for this.

532
00:35:33,798 --> 00:35:35,733
- He started it.
- BORIS: <i>It's a lie.</i>

533
00:35:35,900 --> 00:35:37,493
The cwub is on our territory.

534
00:35:37,669 --> 00:35:40,070
"Cwub"? What's a "cwub"?

535
00:35:40,238 --> 00:35:41,262
Cwub.

536
00:35:41,439 --> 00:35:43,601
What's a "cwub"? I mean,
can anyone understand him?

537
00:35:43,775 --> 00:35:45,471
- Do you know what a "cwub" is?
- Cwub.

538
00:35:45,644 --> 00:35:46,839
Enough!

539
00:35:48,013 --> 00:35:49,242
We will work something out.

540
00:35:49,414 --> 00:35:53,476
Now, this is his territory. What
are you willing to give him?

541
00:36:03,528 --> 00:36:05,156
Boop. (CHUCKLES)

542
00:36:06,064 --> 00:36:07,430
That is not helpful.

543
00:36:07,599 --> 00:36:10,398
Are you telling me you don't
see what's going on here?

544
00:36:10,568 --> 00:36:12,332
He is behind this.

545
00:36:13,238 --> 00:36:14,399
What're you talking about?

546
00:36:14,572 --> 00:36:16,507
He sent this ding
dong to squeeze us,

547
00:36:16,675 --> 00:36:18,507
hoping it would
send us back to you,

548
00:36:18,677 --> 00:36:22,170
so that he could lord it
over Tabby. Ain't that right?

549
00:36:22,347 --> 00:36:25,806
(SCOFFS) That's
just... That's crazy.

550
00:36:25,984 --> 00:36:28,283
She's crazy. She
was in Arkham, hello?

551
00:36:28,453 --> 00:36:29,944
Hello? So was I.

552
00:36:31,122 --> 00:36:32,385
Is that true, Butch?

553
00:36:36,461 --> 00:36:37,724
Unbelievable.

554
00:36:47,539 --> 00:36:50,270
Fine. Run your club.

555
00:36:50,442 --> 00:36:51,637
Just so we're clear,

556
00:36:51,810 --> 00:36:55,042
the only reason you
are alive is Butch.

557
00:36:55,213 --> 00:36:58,206
The moment he gives
me the word, you're mine.

558
00:37:05,423 --> 00:37:06,789
(CLICKS TONGUE)

559
00:37:10,028 --> 00:37:11,028
(SNARLING)

560
00:37:16,401 --> 00:37:17,994
Hello again.

561
00:37:19,237 --> 00:37:20,796
I know why you brought me here.

562
00:37:20,972 --> 00:37:25,000
Your body is beginning to reject
the changes we made to your DNA.

563
00:37:25,176 --> 00:37:30,012
You feel it every time
you use your ability.

564
00:37:30,181 --> 00:37:32,582
How do I fix it?

565
00:37:32,751 --> 00:37:34,617
Stop using the power.

566
00:37:34,786 --> 00:37:37,688
Every time you use it,
new cells are activated,

567
00:37:37,856 --> 00:37:42,351
and your body rejects them.
Stop, and you will recover.

568
00:37:42,527 --> 00:37:44,553
It's that simple.

569
00:37:44,729 --> 00:37:46,357
It's just...

570
00:37:46,531 --> 00:37:49,433
I like the new me.

571
00:37:49,601 --> 00:37:54,266
I can't fix you. I can't
re-order your DNA.

572
00:37:56,875 --> 00:37:59,606
There's always a way.

573
00:38:00,945 --> 00:38:03,676
Strange. He can.

574
00:38:04,682 --> 00:38:06,617
- He's the only one.
- (GROANS)

575
00:38:09,788 --> 00:38:11,256
Where is Strange?

576
00:38:11,422 --> 00:38:13,050
I don't know.

577
00:38:13,224 --> 00:38:14,920
They've hidden him
somewhere secret.

578
00:38:15,093 --> 00:38:18,222
Him fixing me is
just the beginning.

579
00:38:19,531 --> 00:38:20,726
I want an army.

580
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:24,162
I want an army like me!

581
00:38:24,335 --> 00:38:26,702
And he is going
to give it to me.

582
00:38:26,871 --> 00:38:29,898
- He can't.
- Oh, he will.

583
00:38:31,142 --> 00:38:32,735
Or he will die.

584
00:38:35,613 --> 00:38:38,708
You remember Marv.
He's one of yours.

585
00:38:39,918 --> 00:38:44,413
Sort of a fountain
of youth in reverse.

586
00:38:49,294 --> 00:38:50,455
(GASPS, WHIMPERS)

587
00:38:51,496 --> 00:38:52,896
Good night, Ethel.

588
00:38:53,932 --> 00:38:55,867
(WHIMPERING)

589
00:38:58,570 --> 00:39:00,232
(GROANING)

590
00:39:18,957 --> 00:39:20,289
We caught a spy.

591
00:39:21,192 --> 00:39:22,524
- Ivy?
- Selina.

592
00:39:22,694 --> 00:39:25,220
Tell this creep to let go of me.

593
00:39:25,396 --> 00:39:26,591
She's my friend.

594
00:39:27,899 --> 00:39:30,596
- I don't like spies.
- She's not a spy.

595
00:39:30,768 --> 00:39:32,669
Ivy, what're you doing here?

596
00:39:32,837 --> 00:39:35,306
I followed you the other day,
so I knew where you went.

597
00:39:35,473 --> 00:39:37,913
Bruce Wayne came looking for
you, but he was acting all weird.

598
00:39:37,976 --> 00:39:40,070
Who else have you told about us?

599
00:39:40,245 --> 00:39:41,543
- No one.
- I asked her.

600
00:39:41,713 --> 00:39:43,147
- Selina...
- Ivy, shut up.

601
00:39:43,314 --> 00:39:45,326
They're those monsters
everyone's talking about, aren't they?

602
00:39:45,350 --> 00:39:49,014
You better tell your friend to be
careful who she calls a monster.

603
00:39:49,187 --> 00:39:51,816
You better stay away
from me. All of you. I'll tell.

604
00:39:56,427 --> 00:39:57,759
Marv.

605
00:39:59,998 --> 00:40:01,057
SELINA: No!

606
00:40:02,066 --> 00:40:03,364
Leave her alone.

607
00:40:03,534 --> 00:40:04,866
IVY: Stay away from me!

608
00:40:09,207 --> 00:40:11,233
Ivy. Ivy!

609
00:40:16,214 --> 00:40:17,375
Ivy!

610
00:40:19,183 --> 00:40:20,378
Watch out!

611
00:40:21,819 --> 00:40:22,912
Help!

612
00:40:24,289 --> 00:40:25,289
(SCREAMS)

613
00:40:25,523 --> 00:40:26,786
(SPLASHING)

614
00:40:27,959 --> 00:40:29,154
Ivy.

615
00:40:34,165 --> 00:40:35,895
(SOBBING)

616
00:41:01,859 --> 00:41:04,055
(PEOPLE CHATTERING)

617
00:41:31,556 --> 00:41:33,367
ALFRED: <i>Right. Once this
alarm is set, Master Bruce,</i>

618
00:41:33,391 --> 00:41:35,917
no coming downstairs till
the morning. Is that clear?

619
00:41:36,094 --> 00:41:38,461
Yes. But was a new alarm
system really necessary?

620
00:41:38,629 --> 00:41:42,828
I don't know. Was it really necessary
offering a challenge to a shadowy cabal?

621
00:41:44,268 --> 00:41:46,260
Yes, it was necessary,
Master Bruce.

622
00:42:22,106 --> 00:42:24,200
(BOTH GRUNTING)

623
00:42:57,408 --> 00:42:58,569
BRUCE: <i>Alfred!</i>

624
00:43:02,080 --> 00:43:03,104
Alfred!

625
00:43:06,050 --> 00:43:08,076
Alfred, wake up. Alfred!

626
00:43:09,654 --> 00:43:11,418
(STRAINING)

627
00:43:29,774 --> 00:43:31,800
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

628
00:44:04,442 --> 00:44:05,442
English -SDH
